Welcome to the war table. A module is one page in the sidebar of GGE Command. Each module edits one or more {% term id="plugin" %}plugins{% /term %}, the jobs your bot does. Pick a module, pick the account at the top, change its settings and save.

{% terms_on_page /%}

{% screenshot id="sidebar" alt="The sidebar of GGE Command with the Attacks and gear group open. Each module is one page, and a Soon tag marks a module that is not built yet." /%}

A module with several plugins shows them as tabs, as a panel for each kingdom, or one below the other. Each plugin keeps its own switch on the {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card or in its panel.

## Account manager {% #account-manager %}

- [Wheel spin](/modules/wheel-spin/) spins the event wheels with the tickets you hold, keeps a reserve and stops at your daily limit.
- [Messages](/modules/messages/) copies your alliance chat to a Discord channel and sends what you write there back to the game.

## Attacks and gear {% #attacks-and-gear %}

- [Towers](/modules/towers/) attacks Robber Baron towers in all four kingdoms, each kingdom with its own switch.
- [Fortress](/modules/fortress/) attacks the fortresses in Burning Sands, Everwinter Glacier and Fire Peaks.
- [Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo](/modules/nom-sam-daimyo/) attacks Nomad and Samurai camps during their events.
- [Storms](/modules/storms/) attacks the Storm Islands fortresses and sends mead to your Storm Islands castle.
- [Khan](/modules/khan/) attacks {% term id="khan-camp" %}Khan camps{% /term %} during the Khan event, taunts the Khan and can refill your defence.
- [Green Berimond](/modules/green-berimond/) attacks the camps of the Berimond Invasion event with event tools.
- [Invasion events](/modules/invasion-events/) attacks Foreign Lords and Bloodcrow camps for glory.
- [Virtual presets](/modules/virtual-presets/) saves attack waves under a name, so any attack module can send them.
- [Armourer](/modules/armourer/) buys siege tools with coins when a castle runs low.

## Utilities {% #utilities %}

- [Recruit, tools and heal](/modules/recruit-tools-heal/) keeps each castle's troops and tools at the stock you set.
- [Refinery and toolsmith](/modules/refinery-toolsmith/) builds siege tools in your workshops up to the stock you set.
- [Auto-feast](/modules/auto-feast/) starts feasts in castles that hold more food than they need.
- [Equip sell](/modules/equip-sell/) sells loose equipment and gems from storage, never relic or set pieces.
- [Daily chores](/modules/daily-chores/) claims the login bonus, sends the tax collector out and asks your alliance for help.

## PvP {% #pvp %}

- [Alert and autostation](/modules/alert-autostation/) moves a castle's troops to a protected alliance castle before a player's attack lands.

## Discord {% #discord %}

- [Discord attack alerts](/modules/discord-attacks/) posts attacks on you, and your own attacks, to Discord channels.
- [Discord event alerts](/modules/discord-events/) keeps one Discord message up to date each for the fortresses, the Aquamarine Islands and the Aquamarine Towers.

## Account settings are not a module {% #account-settings %}

The pause between attacks, the daily attack limit, the time skips the bot may spend and the shutoff timer belong to the account, not to a module. Edit them on the {% ui key="client:drawer.accountSettings" /%} tab of the account. See [Open an account](/war-room/dashboard/#account-drawer).

## The attack cap {% #attack-cap %}

Your {% term id="attack-cap" %}attack cap{% /term %} is the most attack plugins one account can have on at once. It is 4, 6 or no limit. GGE Command sets it for your user, and it applies to each of your accounts on its own. If no one changed it, it is 4.

The cap counts plugins, not modules. Several modules share it because many modules hold more than one attack plugin:

- Towers has one attack plugin for each kingdom, so up to 4.
- Fortress has one for each kingdom, so up to 3.
- Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo has 2, and Invasion events has 2.
- Storms, Khan and Green Berimond have 1 each. The **Mead replace** tab of Storms does not count.
- Armourer, Virtual presets and the modules outside Attacks and gear do not count.

So with a cap of 4, all four Towers kingdoms leave room for nothing else. The {% ui key="client:module.status" /%} card of each attack module shows how many attack plugins are on and your cap. When you reach the cap, the other switches lock and show {% ui key="client:plugins.attackLimitReached" /%}.

If you save more attack plugins than the cap allows, the save fails. If an account already has too many on, its bot does not start.

## Ideas every attack page shares {% #shared %}

### Source castle {% #source-castle %}

The source castle is the castle an attack leaves from. On Towers and on Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo, you pick it in **Castle to attack from**. Left empty, the bot uses the main castle there. If the castle you picked is gone, the bot falls back to the main castle and the status tells you.

Other modules leave from a fixed castle. Fortress uses your castle in each kingdom, and Storms uses your Storm Islands castle. Khan, Green Berimond and Invasion events use your main castle in the Great Empire.

### Commanders {% #commanders %}

Every attack module has one {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.title" /%} card. It holds one list for every attack on the page.

- Click the tiles in the order the bot should send each {% term id="commander-game" %}commander{% /term %}. Click a picked tile again to take it out.
- {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.all" /%} picks every commander, and {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.clear" /%} picks none. With none picked, the bot sends any of your commanders, in the order that suits each attack.
- Dimmed numbers are commanders you don't have yet. The bot skips them until you do.
- The bot uses each commander for one attack at a time. While a commander marches, the next free one in your list goes.

The picker also has a VIP tile and a {% ui key="client:plugins.commanderPicker.vipCap" /%}, the most VIP commanders the bot may use each day. It never goes beyond the free daily allowance of your VIP level. The bot saves the cap now but does not use VIP commanders yet. {% status kind="planned" /%}

### Army: Autofill or Waves {% #army %}

Every attack module has an **Army** setting with two choices.

- {% ui key="client:army.mode.autofill" /%} lets the bot fill each attack from the castle's troops and tools. The settings below it, such as sides, waves, tools and **Unit order**, steer how it fills.
- {% ui key="client:army.mode.waves" /%} sends exactly the waves you write. Write them on the page, or pick a [virtual preset](/modules/virtual-presets/) to reuse the same waves on several pages.

A plan in Waves is never swapped for Autofill behind your back. If the waves can't be sent as written, the module stops and the status says why.

### Tools {% #tools %}

Most attack modules put siege tools in the first wave, and event tools in later waves during events. Some modules can also buy tools from the armourer for their own castle when it runs low. The [Armourer](/modules/armourer/) module does the same for any castle you list.

### Log only {% #log-only %}

Khan, Storms, Green Berimond, Invasion events and Nomads, Samurai and Daimyo have a **Log only** setting. With it on, the bot builds each attack and writes it to the {% term id="log" %}log{% /term %}, but sends nothing to the game. Towers and Fortress don't have it. See [Test with Log only first](/playing-it-safe/#log-only).

### Distances in clicks {% #clicks %}

GGE Command measures map distances in clicks, one square of the map. **Search radius** on Towers is how far from the source castle the bot looks for targets. With **Horse** set to **By distance**, targets farther than **Feather beyond** get a fast horse feather and nearer ones get the coin horse.

### Daily caps and other limits {% #limits %}

- The account's **Daily attack limit** counts the attacks of every attack module. It is 3,500 by default and at most 4,000, the game's own limit for 24 hours.
- Every attack module of an account shares a limit of 600 attacks an hour.
- Towers has **Most attacks a day** and **Attacks an hour** for each kingdom.
- Nomads and Samurai have **Attacks per run** and **Time skips a day**.
- Khan, Nomads, Samurai and Invasion events can stop at a score you set.

## Modules still to come {% #soon %}

Modules marked Soon in the app have no page here yet. They are: {% ui key="client:modules.live-view.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.castle-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.offer-buyer.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.overseers.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.food-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.rift-raid.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.berimond.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.leveller.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.blacksmith-event-shops.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.coin-farmer.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.bth-blacksmith.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.influence-farming.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.recruiter.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.castle-builder.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.equipment-manager.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.or-storms.name" /%}, {% ui key="client:modules.mp-builder.name" /%} and {% ui key="client:modules.asset-monitor.name" /%}.

Each one has a page in the app that says what it will do. Choose {% ui key="client:module.soon.discord" /%} on that page to tell us you want it.

